{title: The Tent Peg and the Sword}
{subtitle: Judges 4:2–3; 4:6–7; 4:14–16; 4:17–18; 4:21–22; 5:24–28}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] [Bbmaj7] | [Eb] | [Bb] [Bbmaj7] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Israel cried out to the Lord [Bbmaj7]in distress
Oppressed [Gm]for twenty years by iron char[Eb]iots
Sisera com[Bb]manded the army of Jabin
[Dm7]Cruelty ruled from Hazor [Gm]to the plain
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
Deborah called Barak to [Eb]Mount [Bb]Tabor
Ten thousand men from Zebu[Dm7]lun and Naphtali
[Gm]The Lord would draw Sisera [Eb]to Kishon
And [Bb]give the enemy into their [Dm7]hand
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Sise[Gm]ra fled on foot in the [Eb]night
To the [Bb]tent of Jael the Ken[F]ite
She said [Gm]turn aside and do not [Eb]fear
And covered [Bb]him with a blanket
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]He asked for water but got [Eb]milk
In a bowl fit for [Bb]a prince
But her hand reached for [Dm7]the tent peg
And her right hand for [Gm]the hammer
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Sisera [Eb]fled on foot in the night
To the tent [Bb]of Jael the Ken[F]ite
She said [Gm]turn aside and do not [Eb]fear
And covered [Bb]him with a blanket
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[F]She struck Sisera and crushed [Eb]his head
[Bb]Shattered and pierced his tem[F]ple
[Gm]At her feet he sank and [Eb]fell
[Bb]And there he lay [F]dead
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Sisera fled [Gm]on foot in the [Eb]night
To the tent [Bb]of Jael the Kenite
She [F]said turn a[Gm]side and do not fear
And [Eb]covered him with [Bb]a blanket
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[F]His mother looked through the [Eb]window
[Bb]Wailing why the char[F]iot is late [Gm][Eb]
{end_of_verse}
